      "canonicalType": "KnowledgeStatement",
      "label": "属性断言：It is sometimes desirable to retain the dominant poles of the original system, G_H(s), in the low-order model. This can be accomplished by specifying the denominator of G_L(s) to be the dominant poles of G_H(s) and allowing the numerator of G_L(s) to be subject to approximation.",
